From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Arun Iyengar <aiyengar1990@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 6 Nov 2026 15:18:05 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Revert "panfrost: don't describe tilebuffer-reading fragments
 as opaque (v6/v7)"

This reverts commit dc7266d584bfbe576f5c4fb12b64be8105d1b7f9.

The mixedSequence failure it targeted was a fragment job running longer
than the kernel's 500 ms job watchdog (whole 16x16 tiles never written,
gpu sched timeout status ACTIVE), not a descriptor problem. With the
kernel soft-stop/resume series the test passes on Mali-G31 with stock
Mesa and with every old-descriptor debug knob, so the descriptor changes
and the PAN_MESA_DEBUG knobs are not needed.

Generated-by: LLM
